# cleanup-cannot-wait.bot -- reproducer (MANAGED-SUBPROCESS-AND-EVENT-LOOP-
# CENSUS-MILESTONE-1.md, section 8): a resource's cleanup cannot wait on the
# event loop, so a scope-bound child process cannot be terminated
# gracefully (SIGTERM, a grace period, SIGKILL) inside its owner's cleanup.
# The census's module hands the dying child to a reaper task instead.
#
#   tclsh9.0 main.tcl -check audit/managed-subprocess/repro/cleanup-cannot-wait.bot
#   expected: RESOURCE-DECLARATION (a cleanup never yields)
import cleanup_job
import std::event_loop

with context std::event_loop::create(4)
j = cleanup_job::make()
0
